1. Version Control
Version control is a system that helps developers track changes made to their code over time.

2. Repository (Repo)
A repository is a storage location where a project's files and their change history are kept.

3. Commit
A commit is a saved record of changes made to a project.
Whenever you make important changes to your code, you can commit them to save a snapshot of the project at that point.

4. Branch
A branch is a separate line of development within a repository.

5. Merge
Merge means combining changes from one branch into another branch.
